## Key performance indicators
| KPI | Value |
|---|---:|
| Revenue | $275,230 |
| Units sold | 8,162 |
| Orders | 1,000 |
| Average order value | $275.23 |
| Revenue 2022 | $195,575 |
| Revenue 2023 | $79,655 |
| Year-on-year change displayed | -59.27% |

**Interpretation note:** 2022 and 2023 are partial calendar years in this dataset. The -59.27% calculation compares the revenue recorded in 2023 (January–March) with the revenue recorded in 2022 (April–December), so it should not be presented as a like-for-like annual performance decline. A fairer comparison would compare January–March 2023 with January–March 2022, if the latter period exists in the data; it does not in this dataset. Present the figure as a difference between the two calendar-year portions represented, not as a full-year YoY growth rate.

## Data quality
- `transaction_type` contains 107 missing values (10.7% of rows). These were change to "not specified" while these unknown values were not possible to fill
- Dates are represented with mixed separators (`-` and `/`). They parse consistently as month-first dates (`MM-DD-YYYY` or `MM/DD/YYYY`) to produce the dataset period April 2022–March 2023.
- `transaction_amount` equals `item_price × quantity` for all 1000 rows.
- No exact duplicate rows were found.
- `order_id` has 1000 distinct values.

